LSFD(1)                          User Commands                         LSFD(1)



NNAAMMEE
       lsfd - list file descriptors

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
       llssffdd [option]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       llssffdd is intended to be a modern replacement for llssooff(8) on Linux
       systems. Unlike llssooff, llssffdd is specialized to Linux kernel; it supports
       Linux specific features like namespaces with simpler code. llssffdd is not
       a drop-in replacement for llssooff; they are different in the command line
       interface and output formats.

       llssffdd uses Libsmartcols for output formatting and filtering. See the
       description of ----oouuttppuutt option for customizing the output format, and
       ----ffiilltteerr option for filtering.

OOPPTTIIOONNSS
       --ll, ----tthhrreeaaddss
           List in threads level.

       --JJ, ----jjssoonn
           Use JSON output format.

       --nn, ----nnoohheeaaddiinnggss
           Don’t print headings.

       --oo, ----oouuttppuutt _l_i_s_t
           Specify which output columns to print. See the OOUUTTPPUUTT CCOOLLUUMMNNSS
           section for details of available columns.

           The default list of columns may be extended if _l_i_s_t is specified in
           the format _+_l_i_s_t (e.g., llssffdd --oo ++DDEELLEETTEEDD).

       --rr, ----rraaww
           Use raw output format.

       ----nnoottrruunnccaattee
           Don’t truncate text in columns.

       --pp, ----ppiidd _p_i_d_s
           Collect information only for specified processes. _p_i_d_s is a list of
           pids. A comma or whitespaces can be used as separators. You can use
           this option with ppiiddooff(1). See FFIILLTTEERR EEXXAAMMPPLLEESS.

           Both --QQ option with an expression including PID, e.g. -Q (PID ==
           1), and --pp option, e.g. -p 1, may print the same output but using
           --pp option is much more efficient because --pp option works at a much
           earlier stage of processing than the --QQ option.

       --QQ, ----ffiilltteerr _e_x_p_r
           Print only the files matching the condition represented by the
           _e_x_p_r. See also FFIILLTTEERR EEXXAAMMPPLLEESS.

       --CC, ----ccoouunntteerr _l_a_b_e_l:_f_i_l_t_e_r___e_x_p_r
           Define a custom counter used in ----ssuummmmaarryy output. llssffdd makes a
           counter named _l_a_b_e_l. During collect information, llssffdd counts files
           matching _f_i_l_t_e_r___e_x_p_r, and stores the counted number to the counter
           named _l_a_b_e_l. llssffdd applies filters defined with ----ffiilltteerr options
           before counting; files excluded by the filters are not counted.

           See FFIILLTTEERR EEXXPPRREESSSSIIOONN about _f_i_l_t_e_r___e_x_p_r. _l_a_b_e_l should not include _{
           nor _:. You can define multiple counters by specifying this option
           multiple times.

           See also CCOOUUNNTTEERR EEXXAAMMPPLLEESS.

       ----ssuummmmaarryy[=_w_h_e_n]
           This option controls summary lines output. The optional argument
           _w_h_e_n can be oonnllyy, aappppeenndd or nneevveerr. If the _w_h_e_n argument is omitted,
           it defaults to oonnllyy.

           The summary reports counters. A counter consists of a label and an
           integer value. ----ccoouunntteerr is the option for defining a counter. If a
           user defines no counter, llssffdd uses the definitions of pre-defined
           built-in counters (default counters) to make the summary output.

           CAUTION: Using ----ssuummmmaarryy and ----jjssoonn may make the output broken.
           Only combining ----ssuummmmaarryy=oonnllyy and ----jjssoonn is valid.

       ----ddeebbuugg--ffiilltteerr
           Dump the internal data structure for the filter and exit. This is
           useful only for llssffdd developers.

       ----dduummpp--ccoouunntteerrss
           Dump the definition of counters used in ----ssuummmmaarryy output.

       --hh, ----hheellpp
           Display help text and exit.

       --VV, ----vveerrssiioonn
           Print version and exit.

OOUUTTPPUUTT CCOOLLUUMMNNSS
